{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nRebar has manual mutation evidence for seven selected behavioral cores, but Gerrit does not detect\nwhen a changed test weakens those contracts. Mutmut changes production code, not tests, so a changed\ntest must select the production shard it covers. The blocking lane will stay narrow; a weekly/manual\nall-shard run will detect broader mapping and tool drift.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis gate protects the seven declared shards in `docs/mutation-testing.md`. It does not claim mutation\ncoverage for arbitrary new tests or the full codebase. An unmatched changed test is reported as an\nexplicit advisory mapping gap, not silently described as covered. Adding a test to a protected shard\nrequires adding its mapping in the same change.\n\n## Design\n\n- Add one machine-readable shard manifest. Each shard declares one production module, its mutmut\n  filter, selected test paths/globs, shared Python test-support inputs, known equivalent survivors,\n  and numeric budgets. Validation proves every current `only_mutate` and selected-test entry is\n  represented. Global support inputs such as relevant `conftest.py`, mutation config, manifest,\n  runner, and lockfile select every affected shard.\n- On a Gerrit patchset, resolve the checked-out commit and its single parent, then inspect additions,\n  modifications, deletions, and both sides of renames. A changed mapped source, test, or support input\n  selects its shard; mutation-infrastructure changes select all shards. An unresolvable parent/diff\n  fails closed. No selected shard is an explicit successful skip with any unmatched tests reported.\n- Run each selected shard in isolated fresh base and head workspaces with an effective per-shard\n  mutmut config. Never share `mutants/` state between shards or workflow runs. Dependency-download\n  caches are allowed, but mutation verdicts are recomputed. This follows the clean-run/base-vs-head\n  pattern used by maintained OSS gates and removes stale-result ambiguity from blocking CI.\n- Pin Python 3.12 and `mutmut==3.7.0`, use `--max-children 1`, pin mutmut timeouts to\n  `(selected clean-test duration + 1 second) x 15`, and cap the job at 30 minutes. Run the selected\n  clean tests before mutation so baseline failures are classified separately.\n- Parse `mutmut results --all true` for every public status and retain raw output; do not rely only on\n  `export-cicd-stats`, whose 3.7.0 JSON omits some statuses. Zero mutants, not-checked, interrupted,\n  suspicious, skipped, segfault, caught-by-type-check, or an unknown status fail.\n\n## Comparison and budgets\n\nFor a test/support-only change, production bytes and mutant identities are stable. The gate blocks any\nbase mutant that was killed but is non-killed on head, any killed-count loss, or any budget failure.\nThis is the direct evidence that a changed test weakened behavior.\n\nFor a source-changing patch, exact mutant IDs and killed counts are advisory because valid edits can\nadd, delete, or renumber mutants. Head still must satisfy the shard survivor, no-tests, timeout, and\nmapped-score budgets below and produce at least one mutant. This matches active OSS practice: exact\nID transitions are useful when comparable, while stable quality thresholds govern changed source.\n\n| Shard | Historical killed | Survivors max | No-tests max | Timeouts max | Score floor |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| signing | 378 | 3 | 110 | 0 | 99.2% |\n| reducer processors | 774 | 5 | 0 | 0 | 99.4% |\n| next batch | 713 | 6 | 208 | 0 | 99.2% |\n| gates | 557 | 0 | 376 | 0 | 100.0% |\n| validate | 443 | 0 | 223 | 0 | 100.0% |\n| compact policy | 7 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 100.0% |\n| push policy | 8 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 100.0% |\n\nEvery survivor must also match a documented equivalent-mutant fingerprint; the count ceiling alone\ncannot bless a different survivor. No-tests allowances remain separate because subprocess tests cannot\nbe attributed by mutmut in-process. A budget may be changed only with the affected source or mapping,\nmeasured base/head counts, and an updated explanation in `docs/mutation-testing.md`; a budget-only\nrelaxation fails.\n\n## False-positive and flakiness policy\n\n- Baseline-test failure is a test failure. Setup/tool failure, zero-mutant execution, and whole-job\n  timeout are infrastructure/configuration failures. Only independently identified download/setup\n  operations may retry; mutation outcomes never retry to green.\n- A new survivor, no-tests result, timeout, score loss, or comparable killed-result loss is blocking.\n  On failure, rerun every head non-killed mutant once for diagnosis. A stable result remains the\n  mutation regression; a changed result is a nondeterminism failure. Either outcome remains red.\n- Equivalent/cosmetic survivors are explicit fingerprints plus numeric ceilings, not fuzzy severity.\n  Low concurrency, deterministic pytest order, fresh workspaces, pinned versions, bounded timeouts,\n  stale-patchset cancellation, and always-published artifacts reduce operational flakes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Gerrit Validate selects exactly the shards affected by added/modified/deleted/renamed mapped\n      source, test, and support inputs; selects all affected shards for infrastructure changes; reports\n      unmatched tests; and fails when the patchset parent/diff cannot be resolved.\n- [ ] Each shard runs clean in isolated fresh base/head workspaces with no persisted mutation verdict\n      cache, pinned Python/mutmut/concurrency/timeouts, and at least one parsed mutant.\n- [ ] Test/support-only changes block on killed-to-non-killed transitions, killed-count loss, any\n      unexpected status, unknown survivor fingerprint, or numeric budget failure.\n- [ ] Source changes treat exact IDs/counts as advisory but block on zero mutants, unexpected statuses,\n      unknown survivor fingerprints, or survivor/no-tests/timeout/score budget failure.\n- [ ] A failing shard reruns head non-killed mutants once for diagnosis; reruns never turn the gate\n      green, and inconsistent outcomes are reported as nondeterminism.\n- [ ] Results and always-published artifacts distinguish skip/mapping gap, baseline test, setup/tool,\n      whole-job timeout, mutation regression, and nondeterminism.\n- [ ] The job participates in Gerrit `Verified`; newer patchsets cancel stale runs. A weekly/manual\n      all-shard workflow uses the same driver, manifest, budgets, and artifact format.\n- [ ] Hermetic tests cover selection including renames/deletions, manifest completeness, base/head\n      comparison modes, budget-update rules, every result/failure class, and vote aggregation.\n- [ ] `docs/mutation-testing.md` documents cadence, current measurements, equivalent fingerprints,\n      no-tests rationale, unmatched-test behavior, and the budget-update rule.\n\n## Verification\n\n    pytest -q tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py\n    python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py\n    make lint\n    make typecheck\n\n## Primary sources\n\n- Mutmut 3.7 configuration, statuses, invalidation, and timeouts: https://mutmut.readthedocs.io/en/latest/\n- Instructor clean archive, pinned tool, timeout, and explicit budgets: https://github.com/567-labs/instructor/blob/main/.github/workflows/mutation.yml\n- DataDog base/head targeted comparison and advisory IDs for source edits: https://github.com/DataDog/dd-license-attribution/blob/main/.github/workflows/mutation-regression.yml\n- PostHog changed source/test targeting and bounded concurrency: https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-python/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n- Trailmark PR/main execution, cancellation, and always-reported results: https://github.com/trailofbits/trailmark/blob/main/.github/workflows/mutation.yml\n- GeoParquet scheduled/manual sweep, setup-only retries, zero-mutant failure, score floor, and artifacts: https://github.com/geoparquet/geoparquet-io/blob/main/.github/workflows/nightly.yml","title":"Gate changed behavioral-test shards with bounded mutation checks"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786420093448655001,"uuid":"a71b5b3c-2a81-4bb2-8c55-4e335c4e1452"}